  "315b3dfb-1958-4a5f-99ee-5c1c94ee0721": {
   "name": "The data behind IPCC AR6 SYR Figure 2.1",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 1.4,
    "extent": [
     -34478035.576546915,
     -20223937.14614873,
     36704425.39241239,
     27231036.833157476
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "markdown",
     "title": "The data behind IPCC AR6 SYR Figure 2.1",
     "markdown": "## From emissions to warming — and the data behind one IPCC figure\n\nThis story follows **IPCC AR6 Synthesis Report, Longer Report Figure 2.1** through the four steps of the IPCC data chain:\n\n| Step | Question | Where to look |\n|---|---|---|\n| **1 · The report** | What is the figure and where does it come from? | ipcc.ch (SYR SPM → Longer Report → Figure 2.1) |\n| **2 · Input data** | Which observations, inventories and simulations were used? | DKRZ, CSIC + the originating institutions |\n| **3 · Intermediate data** | What did authors compute along the way? | DKRZ, CSIC, CEDA + code on GitHub/Zenodo |\n| **4 · Final data** | Which numbers are plotted, and can I download them? | CEDA (WGI), IPCC Data Catalogue (WGIII), CIESIN-SEDAC (SYR) |\n\nEvery stop lists the concrete record (catalogue, DOI, version, files, licence) and a status flag:\n`AVAILABLE` bundled in this project · `ONLINE` link only · `PARTIAL` incomplete / unverified · `MISSING` no record.\n\nUse **▶ Next** to start at Step 1. The companion notebook `ar6_syr_fig2_1_data_story.ipynb` reproduces the four panels from the Step-4 data.",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "b9604cc1-b097-4e14-ae13-a9a22cb00b18": {
   "name": "Step 1 · The report: AR6 Synthesis Report → Figure 2.1",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 11.5,
    "extent": [
     651072.1888501821,
     5794376.870463113,
     715931.1580912173,
     5837616.183290469
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "map",
     "title": "Step 1 · The report: AR6 Synthesis Report → Figure 2.1",
     "markdown": "**Status: `ONLINE` — figure and caption published; image under IPCC copyright policy.**\n\n* Report: *Climate Change 2023: Synthesis Report* (approved 19 March 2023), doi:10.59327/IPCC/AR6-9789291691647\n* Entry point: [Summary for Policymakers](https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/syr/summary-for-policymakers/) → Longer Report Section 2.1\n* Figure page: [ipcc.ch/report/ar6/syr/figures/figure-2-1](https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/syr/figures/figure-2-1)\n* Title: *The causal chain from emissions to resulting warming of the climate system*\n\n**Four panels and their Working-Group sources** (from the caption's traceability tag\n`{WGI SPM A.2.2, WGI Figure SPM.1, WGI Figure SPM.2, WGI TS2.2, WGI 2.1; WGIII Figure SPM.1, WGIII A.III.II.2.5.1}`):\n\n| Panel | Content | Source figure |\n|---|---|---|\n| (a) | Global net anthropogenic GHG emissions 1990–2019 by gas | **WGIII Figure SPM.1** |\n| (b) | CO₂, CH₄, N₂O concentrations, panel heights scaled to warming effect | **WGI Section 2.1 / Figure 2.5** |\n| (c) | Global surface temperature vs 1850–1900 + warmest period of last 100 000 yr | **WGI Figure SPM.1** |\n| (d) | Warming 1850–1900 → 2010–2019 attributed to human / natural drivers | **WGI Figure SPM.2** |\n\nThe SYR is a synthesis, so its data are re-publications of WG data. Steps 2–4 follow those references.",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "6513b44a-b84c-4149-a23d-144bf69a7f9c": {
   "name": "Step 1 · How the IPCC organises data: three tiers, five archives",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 1.4,
    "extent": [
     -34478035.576546915,
     -20223937.14614873,
     36704425.39241239,
     27231036.833157476
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "markdown",
     "title": "Step 1 · How the IPCC organises data: three tiers, five archives",
     "markdown": "## The IPCC Data Distribution Centre (DDC) model for AR6\n\n| Tier | Definition (DDC) | AR6 archive | Identifier pattern |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Input data** | observations, inventories, model simulations the authors started from | **DKRZ** (CMIP6 subset), **CSIC** (Atlas inputs); observational inputs stay with originating networks | `10.26050/WDCC/AR6.*` |\n| **Intermediate data** | products created by authors while processing inputs, with high reuse potential | **DKRZ** `IPCC-DDC_AR6_Supplements`, **CSIC**, selected WGI figures at **CEDA** | `10.26050/WDCC/AR6.IPCC-DDC_AR6_Sup_*`, `10.5285/*` |\n| **Final data** | the numbers plotted in published figures/tables | WGI/WGII → **CEDA**; WGIII → **IPCC Data Catalogue (MetadataWorks)**; SYR → **CIESIN / NASA SEDAC** | `10.5285/*`, `10.48490/*`, `10.7927/*` |\n\nDDC partners: DKRZ (Germany), CSIC-IFCA (Spain), CIESIN (USA), MetadataWorks (UK); CEDA (UK) is the WGI/WGII final-data archive.\nPortal: [ipcc-data.org](https://ipcc-data.org) · Catalogue: [ipcc-browser.ipcc-data.org](https://ipcc-browser.ipcc-data.org)\n\n**Overall status for Figure 2.1 (checked 2026-10-13)**\n\n| Tier | (a) emissions | (b) concentrations | (c) temperature | (d) attribution |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Input | `ONLINE` EDGAR, GCB bookkeeping, Zenodo workbook | `ONLINE` NOAA/SIO/CSIRO/AGAGE/UCI | `ONLINE` HadCRUT5 etc., PAGES2k; CMIP6 at DKRZ | `ONLINE` HadCRUT4.6; CMIP6 DAMIP at DKRZ |\n| Intermediate | `PARTIAL` no DDC record; processed table = Zenodo workbook | `PARTIAL` per-network means inside final file | `PARTIAL` ensemble stats inside final file | `PARTIAL` assessed ranges inside final file |\n| Final (WG) | `AVAILABLE`* WGIII SPM.1 (10.48490/vfxm-tm28) | `AVAILABLE` WGI Fig 2.5 (CEDA) | `AVAILABLE` WGI SPM.1 (CEDA) | `AVAILABLE` WGI SPM.2 (CEDA) |\n| Final (SYR) | `MISSING` | `MISSING` | `PARTIAL` 10.7927/nq55-cr83 (xlsx not yet fetched) | `PARTIAL` 10.7927/b38b-zp83 (xlsx not yet fetched) |\n\n\\* rebuilt from the published Zenodo source because the catalogue site is browser-only.",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "6ed8d747-aea2-4140-9680-fa0c8257a3e6": {
   "name": "Step 2 · Input data — overview",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 4.2,
    "extent": [
     -4665170.525557168,
     2953165.081767911,
     5555726.451903356,
     9767096.400074927
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "markdown",
     "title": "Step 2 · Input data — overview",
     "markdown": "## Step 2 · Input data: what the authors started from\n\nThe DDC archives **model** input at DKRZ (and Atlas inputs at CSIC). **Observational** input is not re-hosted:\nthe IPCC cites it to the producing institution (WGI Annex III, Chapter 2 FAIR tables, WGIII Chapter 2 SM).\n\n| Panel | Input datasets | Holder | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| (a) | EDGAR v6.0 (fossil CO₂, CH₄, N₂O, F-gases, country × sector); CO₂-LULUCF = mean of BLUE, Houghton & Nassikas, OSCAR; harmonised in Minx et al. (2021) workbook | JRC Ispra; Global Carbon Budget; MCC Berlin → Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.6483002 | `ONLINE` (Zenodo workbook used to rebuild panel a) |\n| (b) | Global mean dry-air mole fractions from NOAA GML, SIO, CSIRO, AGAGE, UCI | each network | `ONLINE` (network series are columns of the CEDA final file) |\n| (c) | HadCRUT5, NOAAGlobalTemp-Interim, Berkeley Earth, Kadow et al. 2020 (Ch.2 assessed mean); PAGES 2k (1–2000 CE); mid-Holocene assessment; CMIP6 historical+ssp245, hist-nat | Met Office/UEA, NOAA, Berkeley Earth, PAGES; **DKRZ `IPCC-AR6_CMIP6`** | `ONLINE` |\n| (d) | HadCRUT4.6; CMIP6 DAMIP hist-GHG, hist-aer, hist-nat, historical+ssp245 (Gillett et al. 2021) | Met Office/UEA; **DKRZ `IPCC-AR6_CMIP6`** | `ONLINE` |\n\nNext stops visit the DDC input archive (DKRZ, CSIC) and five originating sites.\nFull tables with links: `data/input/README.md` in the project.",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "c0063cc2-d644-424c-9f5b-3f3243052e8f": {
   "name": "Step 2 · DKRZ Hamburg — the CMIP6 input archive",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 11.5,
    "extent": [
     1078539.0334963528,
     7067141.857122083,
     1143398.002737388,
     7110381.169949439
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "map",
     "title": "Step 2 · DKRZ Hamburg — the CMIP6 input archive",
     "markdown": "**Status: `ONLINE` — complete, citable, CC BY 4.0.**\n\n* Archive: World Data Center for Climate (WDCC) at DKRZ, DDC project **`IPCC-AR6_CMIP6`**\n  — [wdc-climate.de/ui/project?acronym=IPCC-AR6_CMIP6](https://www.wdc-climate.de/ui/project?acronym=IPCC-AR6_CMIP6)\n* Content: the CMIP6 subset used by WGI authors — **65 118 datasets** from ~120 models / 45 institutions\n  (lists compiled from chapter requests; documented at github.com/IPCC-WG1/DDC-AR6-CMIP6-Data-Archival)\n* Granularity: one entry per model × experiment (e.g. *IPCC DDC: CAS FGOALS-g3 model output prepared for CMIP6*,\n  doi:10.26050/WDCC/AR6.C6CMCASFGO); regional subsets also catalogued\n* Relevance to Figure 2.1: panel (c) model envelopes (`historical`+`ssp245`, `hist-nat`) and panel (d) attribution\n  experiments (`hist-GHG`, `hist-aer`, `hist-nat`) are computed from these files\n* Access: *Find data* on the project page → entry → download (registration for bulk access); licence CC BY 4.0",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "d02c3ea5-dca2-4c63-adde-993b6d5e1a3d": {
   "name": "Step 2 · CSIC-IFCA Santander — Atlas inputs",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 11.5,
    "extent": [
     -455888.8275981303,
     5362320.203168563,
     -391029.858357095,
     5405559.515995919
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "map",
     "title": "Step 2 · CSIC-IFCA Santander — Atlas inputs",
     "markdown": "**Status: `ONLINE` — not a direct source of Figure 2.1.**\n\n* CSIC-IFCA hosts the WGI **Interactive Atlas** ([interactive-atlas.ipcc.ch](https://interactive-atlas.ipcc.ch))\n  and, with DKRZ, the DDC long-term archive for input and intermediate datasets.\n* The Atlas re-uses the same observational and CMIP6 inputs regionally; Figure 2.1 is global, so no Atlas product feeds it.\n* Useful for readers who want regional versions of panels (c)/(d) (regional warming, attribution by region).",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "f7eb34bc-99f7-4f46-aad7-35046e06b8ad": {
   "name": "Step 2 · Mauna Loa — CO₂ since 1958 (panel b)",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 11.5,
    "extent": [
     -17351103.98012209,
     2196547.976594136,
     -17286245.01088105,
     2239787.289421493
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "map",
     "title": "Step 2 · Mauna Loa — CO₂ since 1958 (panel b)",
     "markdown": "**Status: `ONLINE` — originating network, cited not re-hosted.**\n\n* NOAA Global Monitoring Laboratory + Scripps Institution of Oceanography records; global means from the NOAA network\n  ([gml.noaa.gov/ccgg/trends](https://gml.noaa.gov/ccgg/trends/), [scrippsco2.ucsd.edu](https://scrippsco2.ucsd.edu/))\n* In the CEDA final file for WGI Figure 2.5 these appear as columns `NOAA_CO2`, `SIO_CO2`, `CSIRO_CO2` (1958/1979–2019)\n* 2019 annual mean: ≈ 410 ppm (NOAA global); growth-rate columns (`*_gr`) are the inset of Figure 2.5",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "11c33272-61b1-415b-a567-23f6a7135185": {
   "name": "Step 2 · Cape Grim — CH₄ and N₂O (panel b)",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 11.5,
    "extent": [
     16074387.638258236,
     -4987315.736142753,
     16139246.60749927,
     -4944076.4233153965
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "map",
     "title": "Step 2 · Cape Grim — CH₄ and N₂O (panel b)",
     "markdown": "**Status: `ONLINE` — originating network, cited not re-hosted.**\n\n* CSIRO / Bureau of Meteorology baseline station; member of **AGAGE**\n  ([csiro.au/greenhouse-gases](https://www.csiro.au/greenhouse-gases), [agage.mit.edu](https://agage.mit.edu/))\n* CEDA Figure 2.5 columns: `AGAGE_CH4` (1987–), `AGAGE_N2O` (1979–), `CSIRO_CH4`, `CSIRO_N2O` (1992–), plus `UCI_CH4` (1978–)\n* 2019 annual means: CH₄ ≈ 1867 ppb, N₂O ≈ 332 ppb (NOAA global)",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "b0ca03f2-dca9-4467-a58f-c64890ff1f3d": {
   "name": "Step 2 · Exeter — the surface temperature record (panels c, d)",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 11.5,
    "extent": [
     -419153.39563635003,
     6551524.861095589,
     -354294.42639531475,
     6594764.173922945
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "map",
     "title": "Step 2 · Exeter — the surface temperature record (panels c, d)",
     "markdown": "**Status: `ONLINE` — originating datasets, cited not re-hosted.**\n\n* **HadCRUT5** (Met Office Hadley Centre / UEA CRU, Morice et al. 2021) — one of four datasets in the AR6 Chapter 2\n  assessed GMST (with NOAAGlobalTemp-Interim, Berkeley Earth, Kadow et al. 2020)\n* **HadCRUT4.6** — the observational basis of WGI SPM.2 / SYR 2.1(d): 1.06 °C (likely 0.88–1.21) for 2010–2019 vs 1850–1900\n* Palaeo context: **PAGES 2k Consortium (2019)** 1–2000 CE reconstruction (doi:10.1038/s41561-019-0400-0) and the\n  Chapter 2 mid-Holocene assessment (0.2–1.0 °C very likely range) — both included in the CEDA SPM.1 final files",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "3c496dd9-1155-448c-85b0-5f9f442c2e42": {
   "name": "Step 2 · Ispra — EDGAR emissions inventory (panel a)",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 11.5,
    "extent": [
     928035.0819438468,
     5728334.03352596,
     992894.051184882,
     5771573.346353316
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "map",
     "title": "Step 2 · Ispra — EDGAR emissions inventory (panel a)",
     "markdown": "**Status: `ONLINE` — originating inventory, cited not re-hosted.**\n\n* **EDGAR v6.0** (EU Joint Research Centre): fossil CO₂, CH₄, N₂O and F-gases, country × sector × year\n  ([edgar.jrc.ec.europa.eu](https://edgar.jrc.ec.europa.eu/))\n* **CO₂-LULUCF**: mean of three bookkeeping models — BLUE, Houghton & Nassikas (2017), OSCAR — from the Global Carbon Budget\n* GWP100 (AR6 WGI Chapter 7 Table 7.15) converts gases to CO₂-eq",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "e9137a42-51b7-4e02-a395-3831e1b0f429": {
   "name": "Step 2 · Berlin — the harmonised emissions workbook (panel a)",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 11.5,
    "extent": [
     1459808.2894633145,
     6873080.144868744,
     1524667.2587043496,
     6916319.4576961
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "map",
     "title": "Step 2 · Berlin — the harmonised emissions workbook (panel a)",
     "markdown": "**Status: `ONLINE` — author-processed input, openly archived (CC BY 4.0).**\n\n* Minx, Lamb, Andrew et al. (2021), *A comprehensive and synthetic dataset for global, regional and national GHG emissions by\n  sector 1970–2018 with an extension to 2019*, ESSD 13, 5213–5252, doi:10.5194/essd-13-5213-2021\n* Data: Zenodo **doi:10.5281/zenodo.6483002** — `essd_ghg_data_gwp100.xlsx` (14 MB, 196 639 rows: ISO × sector × year × gas),\n  `essd_lulucf_data.xlsx` (regional CO₂-LULUCF 1850–2019, three models + mean)\n* Code: github.com/mcc-apsis/AR6-Emissions-trends-and-drivers (R)\n* This project rebuilds global totals by gas from it (`scripts/build_wgiii_spm1_from_essd.py`): 2019 = 59.1 Gt CO₂-eq, +54 % vs 1990, +12 % vs 2010 — matching WGIII SPM.",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "28b1f499-1014-4932-9443-3ba387e049f3": {
   "name": "Step 3 · Intermediate data — overview",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 4.2,
    "extent": [
     -4665170.525557168,
     2953165.081767911,
     5555726.451903356,
     9767096.400074927
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "markdown",
     "title": "Step 3 · Intermediate data — overview",
     "markdown": "## Step 3 · Intermediate data: what the authors computed along the way\n\n| Archive | Collection | Access | What it holds |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **DKRZ / WDCC** | `IPCC-DDC_AR6_Supplements` — \"input/source and intermediate datasets underlying the AR6\", DDC quality-checked | [wdc-climate.de/ui/project?acronym=IPCC-DDC_AR6_Supplements](https://www.wdc-climate.de/ui/project?acronym=IPCC-DDC_AR6_Supplements) | e.g. assessed GSAT projections (Fig 4.11, doi:10.26050/WDCC/AR6.IPCC-DDC_AR6_Sup_GSATPr), sea-level projection distributions |\n| **CSIC-IFCA** | Interactive Atlas regional products | interactive-atlas.ipcc.ch | regional means, indices |\n| **CEDA** | WGI \"intermediate data\" records for Chapters 2, 3, 6, 7, 8, 12, TS | table in github.com/IPCC-WG1/CEDA_IPCC_AR6_WGI_Figures_data | e.g. Fig 2.11–2.29, 3.27, 3.28, 7.3–7.21 |\n| **GitHub / Zenodo** | figure-generation code | github.com/IPCC-WG1 (137 repos), Zenodo \"IPCC AR6 WGI – Figure x.y\" | scripts that turn inputs into final numbers |\n\n**Status for Figure 2.1: `PARTIAL` — no dedicated intermediate record for any of the four panels.**\n\n| Panel | Intermediate record? | Where the processed numbers actually are |\n|---|---|---|\n| (a) | none in DDC | Zenodo workbook (country × sector × gas with GWP100 applied) |\n| (b) | none | per-network global means as columns of the CEDA Fig 2.5 final file |\n| (c) | none | CMIP6 ensemble mean + 5–95 % range as columns of `gmst_changes_model_and_obs.csv` (CEDA SPM.1) |\n| (d) | none | assessed likely ranges per driver in `SPM2b.csv`, `SPM2c_data.csv` (CEDA SPM.2) |\n\nCode: no SPM-specific repository exists under IPCC-WG1; the Chapter 2 and Chapter 3 figure repositories and\nGillett et al. (2021, doi:10.1038/s41558-020-00965-9) document the method.",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "d318e124-65ff-4f69-8bdb-f10947858f68": {
   "name": "Step 3 · DKRZ Hamburg — IPCC-DDC_AR6_Supplements",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 11.5,
    "extent": [
     1078539.0334963528,
     7067141.857122083,
     1143398.002737388,
     7110381.169949439
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "map",
     "title": "Step 3 · DKRZ Hamburg — IPCC-DDC_AR6_Supplements",
     "markdown": "**Status: `PARTIAL` — archive exists; no Figure 2.1 entry found; full list not machine-readable.**\n\n* Project `IPCC-DDC_AR6_Supplements`: intermediate datasets created by IPCC authors, archived long-term with DDC\n  technical quality assurance (checks of completeness, licence, citation, CF names — see redmine.dkrz.de wiki *Intermediate_datasets*)\n* Example entries: *IPCC AR6 WGI assessed GSAT Projections* (Milinski & Marotzke, doi:10.26050/WDCC/AR6.IPCC-DDC_AR6_Sup_GSATPr),\n  *Relative Sea Level Projection Distributions*, *Sea Level Projections global* — all CC BY 4.0\n* Relevant to Figure 2.1? The SPM.1 / SPM.2 ensemble statistics were archived with the **final** data at CEDA instead.\n* TODO: browse *Find data* on the project page (JavaScript list) and note any GMST / attribution entry.",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "82bb277a-b27b-4882-8e52-315b49eee6f9": {
   "name": "Step 3 · CEDA Harwell — WGI intermediate records",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 11.5,
    "extent": [
     -178703.29552287914,
     6701843.0343899,
     -113844.32628184385,
     6745082.347217256
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "map",
     "title": "Step 3 · CEDA Harwell — WGI intermediate records",
     "markdown": "**Status: `PARTIAL` — intermediate records exist for other WGI figures, none for SPM.1, SPM.2 or Fig 2.5.**\n\n* CEDA's AR6 WGI archive (`/badc/ar6_wg1/data/`) has separate *intermediate* records for Chapter 2 figures 2.11, 2.12, 2.13, 2.15,\n  2.23, 2.25, 2.27, 2.29 and for Chapters 3, 6, 7, 8, 12 and the TS (index: github.com/IPCC-WG1/CEDA_IPCC_AR6_WGI_Figures_data)\n* For the Figure 2.1 sources the processing results travel *inside* the final files:\n  `gmst_changes_model_and_obs.csv` (CMIP6 ensemble mean and 5–95 % range for human+natural and natural-only forcing, 1850–2020)\n  and `SPM2b.csv` / `SPM2c_data.csv` (assessed contributions per driver).\n* Chapter 2 input-data folders (`inputdata_ch2_fig02`, `…fig11`, …) show the same pattern: input and intermediate tiers are published only where authors supplied them.",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "bbabe0ed-1cce-40df-a6fa-96a1cce6290d": {
   "name": "Step 4 · Final data — overview",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 4.2,
    "extent": [
     -4665170.525557168,
     2953165.081767911,
     5555726.451903356,
     9767096.400074927
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "markdown",
     "title": "Step 4 · Final data — overview",
     "markdown": "## Step 4 · Final data: the numbers plotted in Figure 2.1\n\n| Panel | Record | Version | DOI | Host | Files | Licence | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| (a) | WGIII *Data for Figure SPM.1* (Lamb et al.) | 0.0.1, 2022-04-04 | 10.48490/vfxm-tm28 | IPCC Data Catalogue (MetadataWorks) | CSV (browser download only) | per record | `AVAILABLE`* rebuilt from Zenodo source |\n| (b) | WGI Chapter 2 *Data for Figure 2.5* (Hall, 2023) | v20221116 | 10.5285/c6f19b27f8e74e98968c17c8e1f74c60 | CEDA | `Data_Figure_2.5.csv` (30 columns, 5 networks), README, License | CC BY 4.0 | `AVAILABLE` |\n| (c) | WGI *Data for Figure SPM.1* (Gillett, Kaufman, Neukom) | v20221116 (supersedes v20210809) | 10.5285/0b2759059ad6474098e40dad73e0a8ec | CEDA | `SPM1_1850-2020_obs.csv`, `SPM1_1-2000_recon.csv`, `spm1_6500_recon.csv`, `gmst_changes_model_and_obs.csv` | CC BY 4.0 | `AVAILABLE` |\n| (c) | SYR LR *Figure 2.1 (c): Changes in global surface temperature* | 1.0.0, 2025-04-10 | 10.7927/nq55-cr83 | CIESIN / NASA SEDAC (catalogue id 8498) | Excel (~15.5 KB) | see record | `PARTIAL` not yet fetched |\n| (d) | WGI *Data for Figure SPM.2* (Gillett, Thorne, Trewin; Szopa, Sitz, Malinina) | v20210809 | 10.5285/c1eb6dad1598427f8f9f3eae346ece2f | CEDA | `SPM2a.csv`, `SPM2b.csv`, `SPM2c_data.csv` | CC BY 4.0 | `AVAILABLE` |\n| (d) | SYR LR *Figure 2.1 (d): Humans are responsible* | 1.0.0, 2025-04-09 | 10.7927/b38b-zp83 (verify) | CIESIN / NASA SEDAC (catalogue id 8493) | Excel | see record | `PARTIAL` not yet fetched |\n| (a),(b) | SYR-level records | — | — | — | — | — | `MISSING` |\n\nAlso: the CEDA record for an *IPCC AR6 Synthesis Report (SYR) dataset collection* (uuid 9177e927…) exists but is **not yet published**.\n\n\\* the official WGIII CSV sits behind a JavaScript-only site; the project rebuilds identical global totals from the Zenodo source workbook.\nNext stops: CEDA (WGI), MetadataWorks catalogue (WGIII), CIESIN (SYR).",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "0fbb3e0a-05fa-4fd2-83b7-4f28044df8cb": {
   "name": "Step 4 · CEDA Harwell — WGI final figure data (panels b, c, d)",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 11.5,
    "extent": [
     -178703.29552287914,
     6701843.0343899,
     -113844.32628184385,
     6745082.347217256
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "map",
     "title": "Step 4 · CEDA Harwell — WGI final figure data (panels b, c, d)",
     "markdown": "**Status: `AVAILABLE` — three records downloaded and bundled in `data/final/`.**\n\nArchive path `https://dap.ceda.ac.uk/badc/ar6_wg1/data/` (BADC-CSV: metadata header, `data` … `end_data`), all **CC BY 4.0**,\neach with `Readme_for_figure_*.txt`, `License.txt`, `00README_catalogue_and_licence.txt`.\n\n* **SPM.1 v20221116** — `spm/spm_01/v20221116/` → panel (c)\n  `panel_a/SPM1_1850-2020_obs.csv` (decadal-smoothed GMST), `SPM1_1-2000_recon.csv` (PAGES2k, with 5–95 %),\n  `spm1_6500_recon.csv` (mid-Holocene 0.2–1.0 °C), `panel_b/gmst_changes_model_and_obs.csv` (annual obs + CMIP6 envelopes 1850–2020)\n* **SPM.2 v20210809** — `spm/spm_02/v20210809/` → panel (d)\n  `SPM2a.csv` (observed 1.06 [0.88, 1.21] °C), `SPM2b.csv` (human 1.07 [0.8, 1.3]; GHG 1.5 [1.0, 2.0]; other human −0.4 [−0.8, 0.0]; natural 0.0 [−0.1, 0.1]; internal 0.0 [−0.2, 0.2]),\n  `SPM2c_data.csv` (per-driver GSAT effect, e.g. CO₂ 0.79, CH₄ 0.51, N₂O 0.09 °C)\n* **Chapter 2 Figure 2.5 v20221116** — `ch_02/ch2_fig05/v20221116/Data_Figure_2.5.csv` → panel (b)\n  1 971 rows, 30 columns: `{NOAA,AGAGE,CSIRO,UCI,SIO}_{CO2,CH4,N2O}` with `_xdate` and growth-rate `_gr` columns\n\nCitation rule (from the licence file): cite the dataset DOI **and** the report component\n(*IPCC, 2021: Summary for Policymakers … doi:10.1017/9781009157896.001*).\nWGI SPM collection record: catalogue.ceda.ac.uk/uuid/ae4f1eb6fce24adcb92ddca1a7838a5c (SPM.1–SPM.10).",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "ea0ca12c-dc9e-4dbd-86b0-467b676ba3a7": {
   "name": "Step 4 · IPCC Data Catalogue — WGIII final data (panel a)",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 1.4,
    "extent": [
     -34478035.576546915,
     -20223937.14614873,
     36704425.39241239,
     27231036.833157476
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "markdown",
     "title": "Step 4 · IPCC Data Catalogue — WGIII final data (panel a)",
     "markdown": "## Step 4 · WGIII *Data for Figure SPM.1* — IPCC Data Catalogue (MetadataWorks)\n\n**Status: `AVAILABLE`\\* — official record exists; identical totals rebuilt from the open source workbook.**\n\n| Item | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| Record | *Data for Figure SPM.1*, version 0.0.1, published 4 April 2022, authors Lamb et al. |\n| DOI | **10.48490/vfxm-tm28** → resolves to `ipcc-browser.ipcc-data.org/browser/dataset?id=437` |\n| Content | global net anthropogenic GHG emissions 1990–2019, Gt CO₂-eq (GWP100-AR6), by gas: CO₂-FFI, CO₂-LULUCF, CH₄, N₂O, F-gases |\n| Format | CSV, \"Data Downloads\" section of the catalogue page (JavaScript application — browser only) |\n| Source | Minx et al. (2021) ESSD, doi:10.5194/essd-13-5213-2021 (EDGAR v6 + bookkeeping models) |\n| Related WGIII records | SPM.2 (regional emissions, id 441), SPM.5 (pathways), WGIII Ch.2 figure data |\n\n**What this project does:** `scripts/build_wgiii_spm1_from_essd.py` downloads the Zenodo workbook (doi:10.5281/zenodo.6483002)\nand writes `data/final/wgiii_spm1/global_ghg_emissions_by_gas_1970-2019.csv`\n(1990: 38.3 · 2000: 42.2 · 2010: 52.6 · **2019: 59.1 Gt CO₂-eq**; shares 2019: CO₂-FFI 64 %, CO₂-LULUCF 11 %, CH₄ 18 %, N₂O 4.5 %, F-gases 2.3 %).\n\n\\* TODO (optional): download the official CSV in a browser and store it next to the rebuilt file for a one-to-one check.",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "f2d2df45-75d2-4b21-8c1a-08229032d53b": {
   "name": "Step 4 · CIESIN / SEDAC — SYR final figure data (panels c, d)",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 11.5,
    "extent": [
     -8260275.688132955,
     4991312.024424727,
     -8195416.718891919,
     5034551.337252083
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "map",
     "title": "Step 4 · CIESIN / SEDAC — SYR final figure data (panels c, d)",
     "markdown": "**Status: `PARTIAL` — records exist for (c) and (d); workbooks not yet fetched; (a), (b) `MISSING`.**\n\nThe Synthesis Report's figure data are catalogued in the IPCC Data Catalogue and hosted by\nCIESIN / NASA SEDAC at Columbia University (DOI prefix 10.7927):\n\n| Panel | Record | Version | DOI | Landing page | File |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| (c) | *IPCC AR6 Synthesis Report LR Figure 2.1 (c): Changes in global surface temperature* — catalogue id 8498 | 1.0.0, 2025-04-10 | 10.7927/nq55-cr83 | sedac.ciesin.columbia.edu/ddc/ar6-syr-lr-fig2-1c/ | Excel, ~15.5 KB |\n| (d) | *IPCC AR6 Synthesis Report LR Figure 2.1 (d): Humans are responsible* — catalogue id 8493 | 1.0.0, 2025-04-09 | 10.7927/b38b-zp83 (search results disagree — verify) | sedac.ciesin.columbia.edu/ddc/ar6-syr-lr-fig2-1d/ | Excel |\n| (a), (b) | no SYR-level record | — | — | — | use WGIII SPM.1 / WGI Fig 2.5 |\n\nOther SYR records on the same host (for orientation): Figure 2.2(b), Cross-Section Box.2 Figure 1(a),(b) (scenario data from the AR6 Scenarios Database, IIASA).\n\n**TODO** (browser needed; SEDAC refuses non-browser connections): download both workbooks, confirm the DOI and licence\non the landing pages, convert to CSV in `data/final/syr_fig2_1/`; the notebook's final cell then compares them with the WGI values.\n\nCEDA counterpart: the *IPCC AR6 Synthesis Report (SYR) dataset collection* record (uuid 9177e927f0664da9bf1e25f57561d0d8) is created but **not yet published**.",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "b1f52c8a-bcf1-4722-91d7-1269e6f6aa54": {
   "name": "Data status at a glance",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 1.4,
    "extent": [
     -34478035.576546915,
     -20223937.14614873,
     36704425.39241239,
     27231036.833157476
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "markdown",
     "title": "Data status at a glance",
     "markdown": "## Where Figure 2.1 stands today (checked 2026-10-13)\n\n| Step | Archive | Panel (a) emissions | Panel (b) concentrations | Panel (c) temperature | Panel (d) attribution |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 Report | ipcc.ch | `ONLINE` | `ONLINE` | `ONLINE` | `ONLINE` |\n| 2 Input | DKRZ `IPCC-AR6_CMIP6` | – | – | `ONLINE` CMIP6 hist/ssp245, hist-nat | `ONLINE` CMIP6 DAMIP |\n| 2 Input | originating institutions | `ONLINE` EDGAR, GCB, Zenodo workbook | `ONLINE` NOAA, SIO, CSIRO, AGAGE, UCI | `ONLINE` HadCRUT5, NOAA, Berkeley, Kadow, PAGES2k | `ONLINE` HadCRUT4.6 |\n| 3 Intermediate | DKRZ `IPCC-DDC_AR6_Supplements` / CEDA / CSIC | `PARTIAL` none; see Zenodo | `PARTIAL` inside final file | `PARTIAL` inside final file | `PARTIAL` inside final file |\n| 4 Final (WG) | CEDA / IPCC Data Catalogue | `AVAILABLE`* 10.48490/vfxm-tm28 | `AVAILABLE` 10.5285/c6f19b27… | `AVAILABLE` 10.5285/0b275905… | `AVAILABLE` 10.5285/c1eb6dad… |\n| 4 Final (SYR) | CIESIN / SEDAC | `MISSING` | `MISSING` | `PARTIAL` 10.7927/nq55-cr83 | `PARTIAL` 10.7927/b38b-zp83 |\n\nLegend: `AVAILABLE` bundled in this project · `ONLINE` published, link only · `PARTIAL` exists but incomplete or unverified · `MISSING` no record.\n\\* rebuilt from the open Zenodo source.\n\n**Service notes:** ipcc-data.org and catalogue.ceda.ac.uk returned intermittent 502/503 errors; SEDAC and ipcc-browser are browser-only.\nData files were retrieved through `dap.ceda.ac.uk` and the Zenodo API.",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  },
  "730c0903-b39a-43f2-b40e-ce39aa9d7795": {
   "name": "How to reuse the data",
   "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
   "visible": true,
   "parameters": {
    "zoom": 1.4,
    "extent": [
     -34478035.576546915,
     -20223937.14614873,
     36704425.39241239,
     27231036.833157476
    ],
    "content": {
     "contentMode": "markdown",
     "title": "How to reuse the data",
     "markdown": "## How to go from any IPCC figure to its data\n\n1. **Read the caption's traceability tag** (`{WGI SPM.1 … WGIII SPM.1}`) — it names the Working-Group figures the panel came from.\n2. **Final data first.** WGI/WGII → CEDA (`10.5285/…`, index at github.com/IPCC-WG1/CEDA_IPCC_AR6_WGI_Figures_data);\n   WGIII → IPCC Data Catalogue (`10.48490/…`); SYR → IPCC Data Catalogue hosted by CIESIN/SEDAC (`10.7927/…`).\n3. **Open the README and licence shipped with the record**; CEDA files are BADC-CSV (metadata header, `data` … `end_data`).\n4. **Need the processing chain?** Look for intermediate records (DKRZ `IPCC-DDC_AR6_Supplements`, CEDA intermediate table) and the code (github.com/IPCC-WG1, Zenodo).\n5. **Need the raw inputs?** CMIP6 at DKRZ (`IPCC-AR6_CMIP6`, DOIs `10.26050/WDCC/AR6.*`); observations and inventories at the originating institutions.\n6. **Cite twice** — dataset DOI *and* report component — and respect licences: data CC BY 4.0, figure images under the IPCC copyright policy (redraw from data).\n\n**In this project:** `ar6_syr_fig2_1_data_story.ipynb` reproduces all four panels live in the browser from the Step-4 files;\n`data/PROVENANCE.md` lists every record; `README.md` lists the open TODOs (SYR workbooks, DKRZ supplements list).",
     "image": ""
    },
    "layerOverride": [],
    "transition": {
     "type": "smooth",
     "time": 2.0
    }
   }
  }
 },
